":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1984-03-22","later-events_catalog":"1984-03-22","stage19_causal_queue":"1984-03-22"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:12468","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) There is established the Presidential Advisory  \nCouncil on the Peace Corps.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Council shall be composed of no more than 15 persons, who shall be  \nappointed by the President. The President shall ¿designate a member to serve  \nas Chairman of the Council and a member to serve as Vice Chairman. \nMembers shall serve at the pleasure of the President.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Council shall advise the President and the Director  \nof the Peace Corps on initiatives needed to promote the purposes of the Peace  \nCorps Act and actions of the Peace Corps which do so.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Council shall submit simultaneously to the President and the Director  \nof the Peace Corps an annual report on its review of Peace Corps activities, its  \nrecommendations concerning those activities, and the activities of the Council.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The heads of the Executive agencies shall, to the  \nextent permitted by law, provide the Council with such information as may be  \nnecessary for the effective performance of its functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Members of the Council shall not receive compensation for their work on  \nthe Council. While engaged in the work of the Council, members may be  \nallowed travel expenses, including per diem in lieu of subsistence, as author­\nized by law for persons serving intermittently in the government service (5  \nU.S.C. 5701-5707).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Director of the Peace Corps shall, to the extent permitted by law and  \nsubject to the availability of funds, provide the Council with such administra­\ntive services, funds, facilities, and other support services as may be necessary  \nfor the effective performance of its functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Notwithstanding the provisions of any other  \nExecutive Order, the functions of the President under the Federal Advisory  \nCommittee Act which are applicable to the Council, except that of reporting  \nannually to the Congress, shall be performed by the Director of the Peace  \nCorps, in accordance with guidelines and procedures. established by the  \nAdministrator of General Services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Council shall terminate two years from the date of this Order, unless  \nsooner extended.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12468#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"49 FR 11139, PDF pages 11-11","sha256":"f3d5cb551e0834964b335cd81f3c7ec808eb28c3d2a2f2618ca1e7daf8a3a030","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1984-03-26/pdf/FR-1984-03-26.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 9 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)","CONFLICT FULL_AND_PARTIAL_EVIDENCE_CONFLICT: EO:12534: the sources read as both a whole and a partial ending"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12468"}
